  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two batteries of emf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and internal resistances&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively are connected in parallel as shown in the figure.&nbsp;Then, which of the following statements is correct?</p>\r\r<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0070_499a74c38e94.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 189px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The equivalent emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is smaller than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The equivalent emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The equivalent emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The equivalent emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> of two cells is between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> always.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The equivalent internal resistance of the two&nbsp;cells between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is the equivalent emf of the two cells in parallel, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo></math>For all values of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
